{"type":"standard","title":"Uru-Eu-Wau-Wau dialect","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Uru-Eu-Wau-Wau dialect</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q10266012","titles":{"canonical":"Uru-Eu-Wau-Wau_dialect","normalized":"Uru-Eu-Wau-Wau dialect","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Uru-Eu-Wau-Wau dialect</span></span>"},"pageid":33373850,"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1338796495","tid":"deda8ce6-0bd5-11f1-8ed4-be54315bb106","timestamp":"2026-02-17T07:54:22Z","description":"Variety of the Kawahib language","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Uru-Eu-Wau-Wau_dialect","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Uru-Eu-Wau-Wau_dialect?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Uru-Eu-Wau-Wau_dialect?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Uru-Eu-Wau-Wau_dialect"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Uru-Eu-Wau-Wau_dialect","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Uru-Eu-Wau-Wau_dialect","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Uru-Eu-Wau-Wau_dialect?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Uru-Eu-Wau-Wau_dialect"}},"extract":"Uru-Eu-Wau-Wau is one of the eight varieties of the Kagwahiva language, a Tupi–Guarani language, Subgroup VI. The name is also spelled Uru-Eu-Uau-Uau, Eru-Eu-Wau-Wau and Ureuwawau, and is sometimes known simply as Kagwahiva.","extract_html":"<p><b>Uru-Eu-Wau-Wau</b> is one of the eight varieties of the Kagwahiva language, a Tupi–Guarani language, Subgroup VI. The name is also spelled <i>Uru-Eu-Uau-Uau</i>, <i>Eru-Eu-Wau-Wau</i> and <i>Ureuwawau</i>, and is sometimes known simply as <i>Kagwahiva</i>.</p>"}